# This working tree is an Obsidian vault; the GitHub repo is only the code.
#
# The rule is an allowlist: everything at the root is ignored, and the few paths
# below are added back. A deny-list would need editing every time a draft, a
# result dump or a set of notes lands in the vault, and forgetting once publishes
# it. This way anything new is private until it is named here.
#
# Tracked: the code, bibliography, repository README, and one concise Gate A findings document.
# Untracked: private correspondence, the literature vault, planning and handoff notes, thesis
# drafts, audits, cluster output, active experiment records, superseded material, and every PDF.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/refs.bib
!/code/
!/01_gate_a/

# Only the concise findings are public. Detailed notes, chronology, and drafts remain private.
01_gate_a/*
!01_gate_a/GATE_A.md

# Inside code/, the same split as before: source and run records are tracked,
# downloaded data and generated figures are not.

# Downloaded datasets. `/*` not `/`: a trailing slash excludes the directory and
# git does not descend into it, so the negation below would never match.
code/data/*
!code/data/imagenet100_wnids_*.json

# Run records are tracked; figures are not.
code/results/*
!code/results/*.json

# Gate A generated many pilots and superseded sweeps. Publish only the four settled records.
# Last match wins, so the exact negations must remain below the broad gate_a pattern.
code/results/gate_a_*.json
!code/results/gate_a_reference.json
!code/results/gate_a_undefended.json
!code/results/gate_a_bwdrel.json
!code/results/gate_a_released.json
code/results/table2_by_rule.json
code/results/pilot20full_analysis.json
code/results/pilot20fullb_analysis.json
code/results/ref20b_analysis.json
code/results/shards/

# Model weights and experiment scratch.
checkpoints/
runs/
wandb/
outputs/
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.npy
*.npz

# Python.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# PDFs are never tracked. They are immutable downloads git cannot diff, and the
# paper set is reconstructible from refs.bib.
*.pdf

# OS cruft.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
